{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1552622-w20-fomori-power-noxious-miasma-question","id":1552622,"title":"W20 Fomori Power: \" Noxious Miasma \" question.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-07-23T16:43:27-07:00","id":1552622,"title":"W20 Fomori Power: \" Noxious Miasma \" question.","content":"Hello everyone!<br /> <br /> I was reading some of the Fomori powers in Werewolf 20. In page 435-436 there is the power &quot; Noxious Miasma &quot;:<br /> <br /> \u00ab<b> Noxious Miasma</b>: The fomor can waft a noxious cloud of toxic spores at will, affecting anyone within arms\u2019 reach (or a yard/meter, whichever is less).<br /> <br /> <b>System</b>: The fomor can use this power once per scene; it requires a Presence + Subterfuge roll (difficulty 8). Each victim within range can oppose this roll with Stamina + Primal-Urge (difficulty 8). One roll is made against all victims within range. For each success by which the fomor\u2019s roll exceeds its victim\u2019s roll, the victim is immobilized for one round. (A point of Willpower can negate these effects for a round.) The resulting effects including coughing, wheezing, tearing up at the eyes, and gagging. Victims are immobilized and incapacitated, although they can defend themselves. \u00bb<br /> <br /> My question is: the roll required is <u>Presence </u>+ Subterfuge. What is \u00ab Presence \u00bb Is it an error? Is it an ability that is not listed in the main abilities?<br /> <br /> I tried a little bit of my Google-Fu, and I even ask Grok AI, on X if it was an error and/or if there was an errata, but I found nothing.<br /> <br /> Anyone can clarify this? Surely I am not the first one to see this...<br /> <br /> Thanks in advance for your time on this matter!\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25337-lightbringer1","name":"Lightbringer1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25337_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-23T17:23:23-07:00","id":1552623,"title":"","content":"It's a byproduct of people getting used to writing for CoD and Forsaken and then going back to (or just getting thrown into) Apocalypse instead. In the other Werewolf, the system says it doesn't have Appearance but in all honesty just kind of squished it together with Charisma to make the Presence Attribute (the others being Manipulation and Composure, which then bled into WoD5). So, use either Charisma or Appearance for this power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-23T19:24:39-07:00","id":1552624,"title":"","content":"Thanks for your answer Saur Ops!<br /> <br /> I have noticed that another Fomori power has the same error: (W20 p. 423)<br /> <br /> \u00ab <b>Echoes of Wrath</b>: The fomor can incite an emotional outburst from a human victim. Some of these monsters fall to the Wyrm by falling prey to a sin or addiction. Pentex subsidiaries in particular excel at enabling such behaviors in their most weak-willed consumers. Under the right conditions, these monsters can elicit similar behaviors from humans lacking in humanity.<br /> <br /> <b>System</b>: This can be attempted once per scene. The fomor rolls <u><b>Presence </b></u>+ Intimidate; the freak\u2019s opponent rolls Willpower (difficulty 6). If the fomor gets more successes than its opponent, that opponent spends one turn for each additional success unable to do anything other than ineffectually acting out on one of the victim\u2019s dysfunctional emotions. If the subject has been indulging<br /> in a product produced by the Pentex Corporation within the last scene, the difficulty of subject\u2019s Willpower roll might be one or two points higher. \u00bb<br /> <br /> <br /> In that situation (Echoes of Wrath), I could understand why a social attribute is in the required roll. (It's related to emotions).<br /> <br /> However, for the fomor power Noxious Miasma, I don't understand why a social attribute is used, and even why Subterfuge is used. It seems to be a physical power (a cloud) that physically affects other people around...<br /> <br /> Anyone has any suggestions to propose a new roll for Noxious Miasma?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25337-lightbringer1","name":"Lightbringer1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25337_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-23T22:18:27-07:00","id":1552628,"title":"","content":"You could make it Dexterity + Medicine, as it requires the Fomori to control where they spread the spores and how to best do so as to affect their targets.<br /> <br /> I don't mind the presented roll, though. It's a quasi-magical power and can be related to the traits it is for any number of whatever reasons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-23T23:33:14-07:00","id":1552629,"title":"","content":"Using incongruous and ill-fitting traits for what might seem straightforward powers is kind of a White Wolf tradition. Up until W20, the roll for Fenris' Bite was Strength + Medicine (as opposed to Primal-Urge)..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-24T10:00:57-07:00","id":1552634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lightbringer1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1552622-w20-fomori-power-noxious-miasma-question#post1552622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Anyone can clarify this? Surely I am not the first one to see this...<br /> <br /> Thanks in advance for your time on this matter!</div> </div> </div> </div>Unfortunately, W20 is full of small errors / oversights such as this one. Personally, I'd use Stamina + Subterfuge as the activation roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28735-greywolf76","name":"Greywolf76","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28735_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}